#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid ""
"A paper craftsperson fits a terracotta joint into a recess in an ivory board."
msgstr ""
"A paper craftsperson fits a terracotta joint into a recess in an ivory board."

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid "Ardo 2.0.1, January 2026"
msgstr "Ardo 2.0.1, January 2026"

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid "Ardo 6.9"
msgstr "Ardo 6.9"

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid "Ardo doesn’t need to do everything. What it does has to be right."
msgstr "Ardo doesn’t need to do everything. What it does has to be right."

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo installs about a tenth of the packages Docusaurus does, and well under "
"half of what it installed in January. VitePress is lighter still. Fair enough:"
" it’s the one I would have settled for."
msgstr ""
"Ardo installs about a tenth of the packages Docusaurus does, and well under "
"half of what it installed in January. VitePress is lighter still. Fair enough:"
" it’s the one I would have settled for."

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo isn’t a business. It’s the tool I wanted, built to the standard I "
"care about, and it already runs every site we have. This essay is me starting "
"on the second half."
msgstr ""
"Ardo isn’t a business. It’s the tool I wanted, built to the standard I "
"care about, and it already runs every site we have. This essay is me starting "
"on the second half."

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid ""
"Ardo started with the usual stack: unified with remark and rehype for "
"Markdown, Shiki for syntax highlighting, TypeDoc for the API reference. All "
"good projects. But I kept coming back to the same thought: why pull in a whole"
" library and its dependency tree when I only need a tenth of it?"
msgstr ""
"Ardo started with the usual stack: unified with remark and rehype for "
"Markdown, Shiki for syntax highlighting, TypeDoc for the API reference. All "
"good projects. But I kept coming back to the same thought: why pull in a whole"
" library and its dependency tree when I only need a tenth of it?"

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid ""
"Beyond that, I’m hoping a few people share that taste and want to help."
msgstr ""
"Beyond that, I’m hoping a few people share that taste and want to help."

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid ""
"But a big name isn’t a guarantee either. Years ago I told people to use "
"Radix UI. Two of the people who built it now work on Base UI. I’ve watched "
"plenty of React libraries go quiet that once looked like the safe choice."
msgstr ""
"But a big name isn’t a guarantee either. Years ago I told people to use "
"Radix UI. Two of the people who built it now work on Base UI. I’ve watched "
"plenty of React libraries go quiet that once looked like the safe choice."

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid "Docusaurus 3.10.2 with the classic preset"
msgstr "Docusaurus 3.10.2 with the classic preset"

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid ""
"Docusaurus is the obvious answer for React docs, and it carries a lot of "
"history. Version 3.10.2 still builds with webpack by default, inside a large "
"ecosystem that’s hard to slim down from the outside. It also never felt like"
" the right home for a marketing site next to the docs."
msgstr ""
"Docusaurus is the obvious answer for React docs, and it carries a lot of "
"history. Version 3.10.2 still builds with webpack by default, inside a large "
"ecosystem that’s hard to slim down from the outside. It also never felt like"
" the right home for a marketing site next to the docs."

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid "Every version a little better"
msgstr "Every version a little better"

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid ""
"For most of my career, when a tool didn’t quite fit, I picked the closest "
"match and moved on. In January I needed documentation for our React projects. "
"A few years ago I would have picked VitePress, made my peace with it running "
"on Vue, and shipped. This time I built my own."
msgstr ""
"For most of my career, when a tool didn’t quite fit, I picked the closest "
"match and moved on. In January I needed documentation for our React projects. "
"A few years ago I would have picked VitePress, made my peace with it running "
"on Vue, and shipped. This time I built my own."

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid ""
"For the first time in my working life, I can take something I don’t like and"
" make it better at scale."
msgstr ""
"For the first time in my working life, I can take something I don’t like and"
" make it better at scale."

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid "I used to settle for second best"
msgstr "I used to settle for second best"

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid ""
"I wanted to know whether “lean” holds up, so I installed each tool into an"
" empty project and counted. This is a snapshot of the packages installed by "
"npm on macOS arm64, measured on disk. It does not measure build speed."
msgstr ""
"I wanted to know whether “lean” holds up, so I installed each tool into an"
" empty project and counted. This is a snapshot of the packages installed by "
"npm on macOS arm64, measured on disk. It does not measure build speed."

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid ""
"I’ve built JavaScript frameworks since the early 2000s: qooxdoo with 1&1, "
"Unify with Deutsche Telekom, and a long list of smaller open-source projects "
"since. After 25 years you see patterns. You look at a tool and know exactly "
"where it will hurt in two years and how it should have been built."
msgstr ""
"I’ve built JavaScript frameworks since the early 2000s: qooxdoo with 1&1, "
"Unify with Deutsche Telekom, and a long list of smaller open-source projects "
"since. After 25 years you see patterns. You look at a tool and know exactly "
"where it will hurt in two years and how it should have been built."

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid ""
"If you run a team, you’re asking a fair question by now: who maintains this "
"when Sebastian loses interest? Docusaurus has Meta and a huge community behind"
" it."
msgstr ""
"If you run a team, you’re asking a fair question by now: who maintains this "
"when Sebastian loses interest? Docusaurus has Meta and a huge community behind"
" it."

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid ""
"If you want to try it, hand this sentence to your coding agent, in a fresh "
"repository or one you already have:"
msgstr ""
"If you want to try it, hand this sentence to your coding agent, in a fresh "
"repository or one you already have:"

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid ""
"In October, Ardo switched to its own Markdown engine, Ferromark, and its own "
"highlighter, Ferriki, both written in Rust. A week later, TypeDoc was gone and"
" Ardo started reading the types itself. Each of those pieces became a project "
"of its own. In our <0>first-render benchmark</0>, Ferriki produced HTML 4.2 to"
" 5.5 times faster than Shiki’s WASM build on the same files. One "
"documentation tool turned into a whole family of Rust tools because every time"
" I dug deeper, I found the next thing I wanted to do properly."
msgstr ""
"In October, Ardo switched to its own Markdown engine, Ferromark, and its own "
"highlighter, Ferriki, both written in Rust. A week later, TypeDoc was gone and"
" Ardo started reading the types itself. Each of those pieces became a project "
"of its own. In our <0>first-render benchmark</0>, Ferriki produced HTML 4.2 to"
" 5.5 times faster than Shiki’s WASM build on the same files. One "
"documentation tool turned into a whole family of Rust tools because every time"
" I dug deeper, I found the next thing I wanted to do properly."

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid "Install"
msgstr "Install"

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid ""
"It follows Ardo’s agent instructions, adapts the tested example, and reports"
" how typechecking, tests, and the build went. You review the result like any "
"other pull request."
msgstr ""
"It follows Ardo’s agent instructions, adapts the tested example, and reports"
" how typechecking, tests, and the build went. You review the result like any "
"other pull request."

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid ""
"Knowing isn’t building, though. Writing a documentation framework from "
"scratch, with a Markdown pipeline, syntax highlighting, API reference, and "
"search, was a team-sized project. So you made the rational call: take the "
"good-enough option and spend your time on the work that pays."
msgstr ""
"Knowing isn’t building, though. Writing a documentation framework from "
"scratch, with a Markdown pipeline, syntax highlighting, API reference, and "
"search, was a team-sized project. So you made the rational call: take the "
"good-enough option and spend your time on the work that pays."

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid ""
"Large, old projects often turn into a monolithic standard. You look at them "
"and wonder how all of that got in, and why nobody minded it growing like that."
msgstr ""
"Large, old projects often turn into a monolithic standard. You look at them "
"and wonder how all of that got in, and why nobody minded it growing like that."

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid ""
"Most of those breaks came from one question I kept asking: what is actually in"
" here, and why?"
msgstr ""
"Most of those breaks came from one question I kept asking: what is actually in"
" here, and why?"

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid "Packages"
msgstr "Packages"

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid "Second best used to be the smart choice"
msgstr "Second best used to be the smart choice"

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid "Size on disk"
msgstr "Size on disk"

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid ""
"So here is what I’d point to instead. Your content stays yours. What you "
"bring is React components, Markdown, MDX, and the types in your code. I "
"don’t see any lock-in there. If you decide differently in a year, so be it."
msgstr ""
"So here is what I’d point to instead. Your content stays yours. What you "
"bring is React components, Markdown, MDX, and the types in your code. I "
"don’t see any lock-in there. If you decide differently in a year, so be it."

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid ""
"So I started small. Something that fit my own projects: MDX in, plain HTML "
"out, and no need to rebuild the same setup for every website we run."
msgstr ""
"So I started small. Something that fit my own projects: MDX in, plain HTML "
"out, and no need to rebuild the same setup for every website we run."

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid ""
"Something changed this year, and it isn’t my taste. When I counted on "
"November 11, about 365 of Ardo’s 787 commits had been written with an AI "
"agent."
msgstr ""
"Something changed this year, and it isn’t my taste. When I counted on "
"November 11, about 365 of Ardo’s 787 commits had been written with an AI "
"agent."

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid ""
"Steve Jobs is often quoted as saying that innovation means saying no to a "
"thousand things. I think about that a lot."
msgstr ""
"Steve Jobs is often quoted as saying that innovation means saying no to a "
"thousand things. I think about that a lot."

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid ""
"Ten months later, Ardo is at version 6.9, every one of our websites runs on "
"it, and I don’t plan to settle again."
msgstr ""
"Ten months later, Ardo is at version 6.9, every one of our websites runs on "
"it, and I don’t plan to settle again."

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid ""
"That’s what second best really was: not a lack of taste, just a lack of "
"hours."
msgstr ""
"That’s what second best really was: not a lack of taste, just a lack of "
"hours."

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid ""
"The agent doesn’t decide what right means. It doesn’t know which "
"dependency annoys me or why a Markdown edge case matters. That comes from 25 "
"years of noticing those things. What the agent changes is the cost of acting "
"on them."
msgstr ""
"The agent doesn’t decide what right means. It doesn’t know which "
"dependency annoys me or why a Markdown edge case matters. That comes from 25 "
"years of noticing those things. What the agent changes is the cost of acting "
"on them."

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid ""
"The first version worked. After that it was iteration, the way Apple ships "
"iPhones: each one only a step, each one better than the last. Ardo went from "
"version 1 to 6 in nine months, and every major version was a clean break."
msgstr ""
"The first version worked. After that it was iteration, the way Apple ships "
"iPhones: each one only a step, each one better than the last. Ardo went from "
"version 1 to 6 in nine months, and every major version was a clean break."

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid "The half we never did"
msgstr "The half we never did"

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid "The honest objection"
msgstr "The honest objection"

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid ""
"The newer tools are well made, but most of them sit on Astro or Vue. We write "
"React. Our docs need our own components, and so do the landing pages next to "
"them. I didn’t want a second stack just for documentation."
msgstr ""
"The newer tools are well made, but most of them sit on Astro or Vue. We write "
"React. Our docs need our own components, and so do the landing pages next to "
"them. I didn’t want a second stack just for documentation."

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid "The numbers"
msgstr "The numbers"

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid ""
"There’s a German saying: <0>Tu Gutes und rede darüber.</0> Do good things "
"and talk about them."
msgstr ""
"There’s a German saying: <0>Tu Gutes und rede darüber.</0> Do good things "
"and talk about them."

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid "VitePress 1.6.4"
msgstr "VitePress 1.6.4"

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid ""
"We’ve always been good at the first half. We’d rather build the next "
"iteration than talk about the last one."
msgstr ""
"We’ve always been good at the first half. We’d rather build the next "
"iteration than talk about the last one."

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid "What I didn’t want"
msgstr "What I didn’t want"

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid ""
"Why I built my own React documentation framework, and what AI agents changed "
"about it."
msgstr ""
"Why I built my own React documentation framework, and what AI agents changed "
"about it."

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid "Why now"
msgstr "Why now"

#: content/articles/second-best.mdx
msgid ""
"You’re right about the community. Open source has a chicken-and-egg problem."
" Without users, nobody maintains a project, and without maintainers, nobody "
"uses it."
msgstr ""
"You’re right about the community. Open source has a chicken-and-egg problem."
" Without users, nobody maintains a project, and without maintainers, nobody "
"uses it."
